WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.549
Previously on Supernatural 22 years ago

00:00:10.584 --> 00:00:11.667
Sammy.

00:00:12.191 --> 00:00:14.081
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can.

00:00:14.116 --> 00:00:14.990
Go!

00:00:15.025 --> 00:00:17.544
Their mother Mysteriously died

00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:19.982
Now two brothers...
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:20.017 --> 00:00:22.267
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:22.302 --> 00:00:24.518
Are on a quest to find their father

00:00:25.464 --> 00:00:26.498
This is dad's book.

00:00:26.533 --> 00:00:28.711
I think dad wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:28.746 --> 00:00:30.762
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.490
The family business.

00:00:32.652 --> 00:00:33.898
I got to find dad.

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:36.472
That's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:55.222 --> 00:00:58.288
Where have you got those amp
up to? A hundred thousand volts.

00:00:58.438 --> 00:01:01.091
Damn. Yeah, I want this raw
head extra freaking crispy.

00:01:01.126 --> 00:01:03.745
Now, remember you only get
one shot with these things.

00:01:04.226 --> 00:01:06.188
So make it count.

00:01:38.989 --> 00:01:40.014
On three.

00:01:40.887 --> 00:01:41.955
One.

00:01:42.444 --> 00:01:43.762
Two.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:45.474
Three.

00:01:49.151 --> 00:01:50.738
Is it still here?

00:01:50.773 --> 00:01:51.888
Okay.

00:01:51.923 --> 00:01:53.803
Okay, hold your sister's hand.
We're gonna get you out of here.

00:01:53.838 --> 00:01:55.470
Let's go, let's go.

00:01:58.938 --> 00:02:00.491
All right, go!

00:02:03.231 --> 00:02:04.683
Sam!

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.480
Sam, get them out of here!

00:02:12.515 --> 00:02:13.860
Here, take this!

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.235
Run!

00:02:25.255 --> 00:02:27.663
Come on!

00:03:05.972 --> 00:03:07.491
Dean!

00:03:08.268 --> 00:03:09.147
Dean!

00:03:09.368 --> 00:03:10.256
Hey!

00:03:10.693 --> 00:03:12.599
Hey, hey!

00:03:22.211 --> 00:03:23.742
Sorry, I'm so sorry to ask.

00:03:23.777 --> 00:03:26.115
There doesn't seem to
be any insurance on file.

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:28.157
Right, um...

00:03:29.869 --> 00:03:31.405
Okay.

00:03:32.865 --> 00:03:36.176
Okay, Mr. Burkevits.

00:03:38.649 --> 00:03:42.279
Look, we can finish this
up later. No, no it's okay.

00:03:42.314 --> 00:03:45.286
We were just taking a short cut
through the neighborhood and um...

00:03:45.321 --> 00:03:48.073
Windows were all down,
we heard some screaming.

00:03:48.108 --> 00:03:50.826
We drove pass the house
and we stopped, ran in.

00:03:50.861 --> 00:03:52.356
And you found the kids in the basement.

00:03:52.391 --> 00:03:53.227
Yeah.

00:03:53.262 --> 00:03:55.508
Well, thank god you did.

00:03:55.917 --> 00:03:59.045
Excuse me. Sure, thanks for your help.

00:03:59.311 --> 00:04:00.256
Hey, doc. Is he...

00:04:00.291 --> 00:04:02.428
He's resting. And?

00:04:02.463 --> 00:04:04.953
The electrocution
triggered a heart attack.

00:04:04.988 --> 00:04:09.709
A pretty massive one. I'm
afraid his heart, it's damaged.

00:04:09.744 --> 00:04:12.386
How damaged? We've done all we can.

00:04:12.421 --> 00:04:15.643
We can try and keep him
comfortable at this point but...

00:04:15.678 --> 00:04:18.866
I'll give him a couple of
weeks at most, maybe a month.

00:04:18.901 --> 00:04:20.397
No, no, there is...

00:04:20.432 --> 00:04:23.278
There's gotta be something you
can do. Some kind of treatment.

00:04:23.313 --> 00:04:25.522
We can't work miracles.

00:04:25.557 --> 00:04:28.200
I really am sorry.

00:04:37.489 --> 00:04:43.107
You ever actually watched
daytime TV? It's terrible.

00:04:44.757 --> 00:04:46.342
I talked to your doctor.

00:04:46.377 --> 00:04:48.790
That fabric soft teddy bear, oh.

00:04:48.825 --> 00:04:51.699
I'll hunt that bitch down. Dean...

00:04:51.734 --> 00:04:53.947
Yeah.

00:04:53.982 --> 00:04:57.743
All right, well. Looks like
you're gonna leave town without me.

00:04:57.778 --> 00:04:59.808
What are you talking about?
I'm not gonna leave you here.

00:04:59.843 --> 00:05:01.713
Hey, if you take care of that car.

00:05:01.748 --> 00:05:03.549
I'll swear I'll hunt your ass.

00:05:03.584 --> 00:05:07.551
I don't think that's funny. Uh,
come on. It's a little funny.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.528
Look, Sam. What can I say,
man. It's a dangerous gig.

00:05:17.563 --> 00:05:19.976
I drew the short straw.
That it, end of story.

00:05:20.011 --> 00:05:22.254
Don't talk like that, all right?

00:05:22.289 --> 00:05:25.256
We still have options. What options?

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:28.154
Get burial or cremation?

00:05:28.189 --> 00:05:31.017
I know it's not easy.

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:34.788
But I'm gonna die.

00:05:34.968 --> 00:05:37.702
And you can't stop it.

00:05:39.695 --> 00:05:41.436
Watch me.

00:05:41.471 --> 00:05:43.935
This is John Winchester.
I can't be reached.

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:46.399
If this is an emergency
call my son Dean.

00:05:46.434 --> 00:05:51.702
866-907-3235.
He can help.

00:05:51.737 --> 00:05:54.474
Hey, dad. It's Sam.

00:05:55.745 --> 00:05:58.111
You probably won't get this but uh...

00:05:58.146 --> 00:06:00.064
It's Dean...

00:06:00.099 --> 00:06:02.803
He's sick and uh...

00:06:02.967 --> 00:06:06.588
Doctors says there
nothing they can do. Um...

00:06:07.874 --> 00:06:09.260
But uh...

00:06:09.295 --> 00:06:12.278
They don't know things
we know, right? Um...

00:06:12.313 --> 00:06:14.942
So, don't worry, cause I'm uh...

00:06:14.977 --> 00:06:18.066
Gonna do everything it
takes to get him better.

00:06:18.982 --> 00:06:20.460
All right.

00:06:20.495 --> 00:06:22.868
Just wanted you to know.

00:06:37.482 --> 00:06:38.811
What the hell are you doing here?

00:06:38.846 --> 00:06:41.818
I checked myself out. Are you crazy?

00:06:41.853 --> 00:06:45.896
I'm not gonna die in a hospital
where the nurses aren't even hot.

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:48.407
You know, this whole...

00:06:48.442 --> 00:06:50.874
I laugh in the face of
death thing... It's crap.

00:06:50.909 --> 00:06:53.199
I can see right through it.

00:06:53.234 --> 00:06:55.158
Yeah, whatever dude.

00:06:55.193 --> 00:06:57.389
Have you even slept?
You look worse than me.

00:06:57.424 --> 00:07:01.160
I've been scattering the
internet for the last three days.

00:07:02.737 --> 00:07:05.780
Calling every contact
in dad journal. For what?

00:07:05.815 --> 00:07:07.608
For what'll help you.

00:07:07.643 --> 00:07:10.699
One of dad's friends
Joshua. He called me back.

00:07:10.734 --> 00:07:13.271
Told me about a guy in
Nebraska. Specialist.

00:07:13.306 --> 00:07:15.808
You're not gonna let me
die in peace, are you?

00:07:15.843 --> 00:07:17.861
I'm not gonna let you die, period.

00:07:17.896 --> 00:07:20.380
We're going.

00:07:40.525 --> 00:07:43.642
The church of Roy Le Grange
Faith Healer. Witness the miracle

00:07:44.945 --> 00:07:47.899
I got you. I got it!

00:07:48.824 --> 00:07:50.756
Man, you're a lying bastard.

00:07:50.791 --> 00:07:52.855
I thought you said we
were going to see a doctor.

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:54.578
I believe I said a 'specialist'.

00:07:54.613 --> 00:07:56.852
Look Dean, this guy's
suppose to be the real deal.

00:07:56.887 --> 00:08:00.322
I can't believe you brought me here to see
some guy who heals people out of a tent!

00:08:00.357 --> 00:08:03.336
Reverend Le Grange is a
great man. Yeah, that's nice.

00:08:03.371 --> 00:08:05.591
I have a right to protest.
This man is a fraud.

00:08:05.626 --> 00:08:08.074
He's bilking all these people
out of their hard earned money!

00:08:08.109 --> 00:08:11.513
This is a place of
worship. Let's go, move it.

00:08:11.548 --> 00:08:13.755
I take it he's not part of the flock.

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:16.176
What would people see something
that they can't explain.

00:08:16.211 --> 00:08:18.563
There's controversy. Come
on, Sam. A Faith Healer?

00:08:18.598 --> 00:08:21.913
Maybe it's time to have
a little faith Dean.

00:08:22.666 --> 00:08:24.733
You know what I got faith in? Reality.

00:08:24.768 --> 00:08:26.966
Knowing what's really going on.

00:08:27.001 --> 00:08:28.548
How can you be a skeptic?

00:08:28.583 --> 00:08:30.010
With the things we see everyday.

00:08:30.045 --> 00:08:32.021
Exactly, we see them.
We know they're real.

00:08:32.056 --> 00:08:33.319
But if you know evil's out there

00:08:33.354 --> 00:08:34.920
How can you not believe
good's out there too?

00:08:34.955 --> 00:08:36.486
Cause I've seen what
evil does to good people.

00:08:36.521 --> 00:08:39.307
Maybe god works in mysterious ways.

00:08:39.868 --> 00:08:41.950
Maybe he does.

00:08:41.985 --> 00:08:44.265
I think you just turned
me Around on the subject.

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:46.349
Yeah, I'm sure.

00:08:46.384 --> 00:08:48.477
I'm Dean. This is Sam.

00:08:48.512 --> 00:08:50.249
Leila.

00:08:50.284 --> 00:08:53.645
Sir, if you're not a believer
then why are you here?

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:57.156
Well, apparently my brother here
believes enough for the both of us.

00:08:57.191 --> 00:09:00.446
Come on Leila. It's
about to start. All right.

00:09:00.481 --> 00:09:02.216
Bye.

00:09:02.483 --> 00:09:05.433
Well, I bet you, she can
work in mysterious ways.

00:09:05.468 --> 00:09:07.561
Ladies and gentlemen, please be seated.

00:09:07.596 --> 00:09:10.889
We're starting in just a moment.
Welcome all faiths True believers revival

00:09:13.204 --> 00:09:16.506
Yeah, peace love and trust all over.

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:22.222
Come on.

00:09:22.257 --> 00:09:23.561
Don't, we're sitting here.

00:09:23.596 --> 00:09:24.998
We're sitting up front.

00:09:25.033 --> 00:09:26.400
What? Why? Come on.

00:09:26.435 --> 00:09:27.927
Oh, come on Sam.

00:09:27.962 --> 00:09:29.384
You're all right?

00:09:29.419 --> 00:09:33.086
This is ridiculous. I'm
good, dude. Get off me.

00:09:34.113 --> 00:09:36.096
Perfect. Yeah, perfect.

00:09:36.131 --> 00:09:38.064
Take it off

00:09:47.786 --> 00:09:52.388
Each morning my wife Sue
Ann brings me the news.

00:09:52.423 --> 00:09:54.939
Never seems good, does it? No.

00:09:54.974 --> 00:09:57.421
Seems like there's always someone

00:09:57.456 --> 00:10:02.863
Committing some immoral,
unspeakable act. That's right.

00:10:02.898 --> 00:10:05.989
But I say to you. God is watching.

00:10:06.024 --> 00:10:07.434
Here, here.

00:10:07.469 --> 00:10:13.987
God rewards the good and he
punishes the corrupt. Right.

00:10:14.022 --> 00:10:18.614
It is the Lord who does
the healing here friends.

00:10:18.649 --> 00:10:23.172
The Lord who guides me
and chosen who to heal

00:10:23.207 --> 00:10:26.788
By helping me to see into
people's hearts. Amen.

00:10:26.823 --> 00:10:29.233
Yeah, rid of their wallets.

00:10:29.268 --> 00:10:31.643
You think so young man?

00:10:33.084 --> 00:10:36.503
Sorry. No, no. Don't be.

00:10:36.538 --> 00:10:41.479
Just watch what you say around a
blind man. We got real sharp ears.

00:10:42.535 --> 00:10:44.929
What's your name son?

00:10:45.567 --> 00:10:48.342
Dean. Dean.

00:10:50.083 --> 00:10:53.871
I want you to come up here with me.

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:03.402
No, it's okay.

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:04.690
What are you doing?

00:11:04.725 --> 00:11:08.618
You come here to be healed, haven't you?

00:11:10.829 --> 00:11:13.647
Oh, yeah but uh...

00:11:13.682 --> 00:11:17.623
Maybe you should just pick someone else.

00:11:20.123 --> 00:11:24.743
I didn't pick you Dean. The Lord did.

00:11:26.224 --> 00:11:28.622
Get up there!

00:11:28.851 --> 00:11:32.994
Yes. Yes. Amen.

00:11:39.236 --> 00:11:40.962
You're ready?

00:11:40.997 --> 00:11:43.800
Yeah, with no disrespect but uh...

00:11:43.835 --> 00:11:46.623
I'm not exactly a believer.

00:11:46.768 --> 00:11:48.653
You will be son.

00:11:48.688 --> 00:11:50.538
You will be.

00:11:50.722 --> 00:11:53.396
Pray with me friends.

00:12:17.068 --> 00:12:21.260
All right now.

00:12:30.258 --> 00:12:32.862
All right now.

00:12:37.311 --> 00:12:39.028
Dean!

00:12:43.885 --> 00:12:45.925
Say something!

00:12:59.256 --> 00:13:01.111
So you really feel okay?

00:13:01.146 --> 00:13:02.464
I feel fine Sam.

00:13:02.499 --> 00:13:06.361
Well, according to all your tests.
There's nothing wrong with your heart.

00:13:06.396 --> 00:13:08.121
No sign there ever was.

00:13:08.156 --> 00:13:11.888
Not that a man your age should
be having heart trouble but uh...

00:13:11.923 --> 00:13:13.902
Still it's strange, it does happen.

00:13:13.937 --> 00:13:15.063
What do you mean strange?

00:13:15.098 --> 00:13:18.711
Well, just yesterday a young
guy like you. 27, athletic.

00:13:18.746 --> 00:13:21.414
I don't know a heart attack.

00:13:22.255 --> 00:13:24.053
Thanks doc.

00:13:24.088 --> 00:13:25.851
No problem.

00:13:27.006 --> 00:13:29.112
That's odd. Maybe it's coincidence.

00:13:29.147 --> 00:13:31.267
People's heart give up all
the time, man. No they don't.

00:13:31.302 --> 00:13:33.352
Look Dean. Do we really have
to look this one in the mouth?

00:13:33.387 --> 00:13:36.021
Why can't we just be thankful that
the guy saved your life and move on?

00:13:36.056 --> 00:13:38.787
Because I can't shake
this feeling, that's why.

00:13:38.822 --> 00:13:40.739
What feeling?

00:13:40.774 --> 00:13:44.204
When I was healed. I just, I felt wrong.

00:13:44.239 --> 00:13:47.510
Felt cold and for a second

00:13:47.545 --> 00:13:49.429
I saw someone. I saw this old man.

00:13:49.464 --> 00:13:51.278
I'm telling you Sam. It was a spirit.

00:13:51.313 --> 00:13:53.922
But if there was something there
Dean. I think I would have seen it too.

00:13:53.957 --> 00:13:56.150
I mean I've been seeing
awful lot of things lately.

00:13:56.185 --> 00:13:57.899
Well, excuse me psychic wonder.

00:13:57.934 --> 00:14:00.865
But you just need a
little faith on this one.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:05.042
Sam, I've been hunting long enough
to trust a feeling like this.

00:14:07.347 --> 00:14:09.334
Yeah, right.

00:14:10.406 --> 00:14:12.649
So what do you want to do?

00:14:12.684 --> 00:14:14.061
Why don't you to check
out that heart attack guy.

00:14:14.096 --> 00:14:16.292
I'm gonna visit the reverend.

00:14:19.221 --> 00:14:20.814
I feel great.

00:14:20.849 --> 00:14:22.372
Just trying to...

00:14:22.407 --> 00:14:24.488
You know, make sense of what happened.

00:14:24.523 --> 00:14:27.415
A miracle's what happened.

00:14:27.794 --> 00:14:32.321
Miracles come so often around Roy.

00:14:33.014 --> 00:14:35.623
When did they start? The miracles.

00:14:35.658 --> 00:14:38.197
Woke up one morning stone blind.

00:14:38.232 --> 00:14:42.564
Doctors figured out I had cancer.
Told me I had maybe a month.

00:14:42.599 --> 00:14:44.157
So uh...

00:14:44.192 --> 00:14:46.448
We prayed for a miracle.

00:14:46.483 --> 00:14:49.063
I was weak but...

00:14:49.098 --> 00:14:52.492
I told Sue Ann to just keep on praying.

00:14:52.527 --> 00:14:54.064
I went into a coma.

00:14:54.099 --> 00:14:56.898
Doctors said I wouldn't
wake up but I did.

00:14:56.933 --> 00:14:59.398
And the cancer was gone.

00:14:59.433 --> 00:15:05.095
If it wasn't for these eyes, no
one would believe I ever had it.

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:07.804
And suddenly you can heal people?

00:15:07.839 --> 00:15:10.412
I discovered it afterwards, yes.

00:15:10.447 --> 00:15:12.950
God's blessed me in many ways.

00:15:12.985 --> 00:15:18.520
And his flock swelled over night.
And this is just the beginning.

00:15:20.156 --> 00:15:22.372
Can I ask you one last question?

00:15:22.407 --> 00:15:24.641
Of course you can.

00:15:25.333 --> 00:15:27.893
Why? Why me?

00:15:27.928 --> 00:15:31.279
Out of all the sick people why save me?

00:15:31.314 --> 00:15:35.090
Well, like I said before.
The Lord guides me.

00:15:35.125 --> 00:15:42.541
I looked into your heart and you
just stood out from all the rest.

00:15:42.705 --> 00:15:46.332
What did you see in my heart?

00:15:46.367 --> 00:15:50.126
A young man with an important
purpose. A job to do.

00:15:50.161 --> 00:15:53.183
And it isn't finished.

00:15:54.908 --> 00:15:59.003
He seemed healthy. Swam
everyday. Didn't smoke.

00:15:59.038 --> 00:16:01.899
It's no so hard to act this
kind of scene. No bizarre.

00:16:01.934 --> 00:16:04.760
And you said he was running?
Right before he collapsed?

00:16:04.795 --> 00:16:06.672
Yeah, yeah. He was freaking out.

00:16:06.707 --> 00:16:08.418
Said that something was...

00:16:08.453 --> 00:16:10.095
After him. Did he say what?

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:13.783
Thin air, that's what. I
mean, there wasn't anything.

00:16:13.967 --> 00:16:15.854
All right, thanks.

00:16:18.309 --> 00:16:19.783
Hey buddy. You're...

00:16:19.818 --> 00:16:21.291
You're clock's busted.

00:16:21.326 --> 00:16:22.730
Oh, yeah. We uh...

00:16:22.765 --> 00:16:27.236
We can't get it working.
Just froze at 4:17.

00:16:27.271 --> 00:16:29.839
Is that the same time Marshall died?

00:16:29.874 --> 00:16:31.731
How did you know?

00:16:35.209 --> 00:16:37.756
Dean, hey. Hey.

00:16:37.953 --> 00:16:39.659
How you feeling? I feel good.

00:16:39.694 --> 00:16:42.091
Cured, I guess.

00:16:42.126 --> 00:16:43.689
What are you doing here?

00:16:43.724 --> 00:16:46.953
You know my mom. She wanted
to talk to the reverend.

00:16:46.988 --> 00:16:48.704
Leila.

00:16:49.738 --> 00:16:53.858
Yes, we're here again. Oh,
I'm sorry but Roy's resting.

00:16:53.893 --> 00:16:56.284
He won't be seeing anyone right now.

00:16:56.319 --> 00:16:58.320
Sue Ann please.

00:16:58.355 --> 00:17:00.998
This is our sixth time.
He's got to see us.

00:17:01.033 --> 00:17:03.213
Roy is aware of Leila's situation

00:17:03.248 --> 00:17:06.367
And he very well much wants to help
just as soon as the Lord allows.

00:17:06.402 --> 00:17:09.694
Have faith Mrs. Roke.

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:19.413
Why are you still even here?

00:17:19.448 --> 00:17:21.502
You've got what you wanted. Mom.

00:17:21.537 --> 00:17:23.365
Stop.

00:17:23.400 --> 00:17:25.976
No Leila this is too much.

00:17:26.011 --> 00:17:28.491
We've been to every single service.

00:17:28.526 --> 00:17:31.441
If Roy would stop choosing
these strangers over you.

00:17:31.476 --> 00:17:34.639
Strangers who don't even believe.

00:17:34.674 --> 00:17:37.802
I just can't pray any harder.

00:17:37.837 --> 00:17:40.448
Leila, what's wrong?

00:17:42.652 --> 00:17:44.944
I have this thing.

00:17:44.979 --> 00:17:47.236
It's a brain tumor.

00:17:47.691 --> 00:17:50.636
It's inoperable.

00:17:50.812 --> 00:17:54.547
In sixth months the doctors say...

00:17:58.982 --> 00:18:01.217
I'm sorry.

00:18:01.751 --> 00:18:03.651
It's okay.

00:18:03.686 --> 00:18:05.666
No.

00:18:05.952 --> 00:18:08.667
It isn't.

00:18:13.865 --> 00:18:18.278
Why do you deserve to
live more than my daughter?

00:18:46.652 --> 00:18:48.991
What did you find out?

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:51.631
I'm sorry.

00:18:51.819 --> 00:18:53.010
Sorry about what?

00:18:53.045 --> 00:18:58.579
Marshall Hall died at 4:17.

00:18:58.797 --> 00:19:01.285
The exact time I was healed. Yeah.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:04.863
So, I put together a list.
Everyone Roy's healed.

00:19:04.898 --> 00:19:08.509
Six people over the past year and I
cross checked them with local obits.

00:19:08.544 --> 00:19:11.245
Every time someone was
healed someone else died.

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:12.666
And each time the victim died

00:19:12.701 --> 00:19:15.572
Of the same symptom Le Grange
was healing at the time.

00:19:15.607 --> 00:19:18.443
Someone healed a cancer,
someone else died of cancer?

00:19:18.478 --> 00:19:21.849
Somehow. Le Grange...

00:19:22.033 --> 00:19:26.226
Is trading a life for another. Hello?

00:19:27.397 --> 00:19:29.101
Wait, wait, wait. So...

00:19:29.136 --> 00:19:31.713
Marshall Hall died to save me?

00:19:31.748 --> 00:19:33.642
Dean...

00:19:33.856 --> 00:19:36.282
The guy probably would have died anyway.

00:19:36.317 --> 00:19:38.708
And someone else would have been healed.

00:19:40.862 --> 00:19:43.230
You never should have brought me here.

00:19:43.265 --> 00:19:45.814
Dean, I was just trying
to save your life.

00:19:45.849 --> 00:19:48.363
But Sam, some guy is
dead now because of me!

00:19:48.398 --> 00:19:51.172
I didn't know.

00:19:52.008 --> 00:19:55.015
Pray with me friends.

00:19:55.857 --> 00:19:59.046
The thing I don't understand
is how is Roy doing it?

00:19:59.081 --> 00:20:01.892
How's he trading a life for a life?

00:20:01.927 --> 00:20:04.674
Oh, he's not doing it.

00:20:04.819 --> 00:20:06.949
Something else is doing it for him.

00:20:06.984 --> 00:20:11.268
What do you mean? The
old man I saw on stage.

00:20:11.658 --> 00:20:13.456
I didn't want to believe
it. But deep down, I knew it.

00:20:13.491 --> 00:20:15.549
You knew what? What
are you talking about?

00:20:15.584 --> 00:20:19.946
There's only one thing that can
give and take life like that.

00:20:19.981 --> 00:20:22.613
We're dealing with a reaper.

00:21:22.521 --> 00:21:24.282
You really think it's the 'Grim Reaper'?

00:21:24.317 --> 00:21:27.303
Like Angel of Death, the
Collector of Soul the whole deal?

00:21:27.338 --> 00:21:29.829
No, no, no. Not 'The
Reaper'. A 'Reaper'.

00:21:29.864 --> 00:21:32.180
There's reaper law in pretty
much every culture on earth.

00:21:32.215 --> 00:21:33.949
They go by a hundred different names.

00:21:33.984 --> 00:21:35.932
It's possible this one's one of them.

00:21:35.967 --> 00:21:37.845
But you said you saw a dude in a suit.

00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:41.845
What? You think he should be
working the whole black robe thing?

00:21:41.880 --> 00:21:44.731
You said it yourself that
the clock stopped right?

00:21:45.635 --> 00:21:47.669
Reapers stop time.

00:21:47.704 --> 00:21:49.190
And you can only see them
when they're coming at you

00:21:49.225 --> 00:21:51.247
Which is why I could
see him and you couldn't.

00:21:51.282 --> 00:21:53.234
Maybe. There's nothing
else that could be Sam.

00:21:53.269 --> 00:21:56.499
The question is how's Roy
controlling the damn thing.

00:21:56.534 --> 00:21:58.190
That cross.

00:21:58.225 --> 00:22:00.624
What? There was this cross.

00:22:00.659 --> 00:22:05.236
I noticed it in the church
tent, I knew I seen it before.

00:22:10.961 --> 00:22:12.812
Here.

00:22:13.356 --> 00:22:14.461
Tarot?

00:22:14.496 --> 00:22:16.046
It makes sense.

00:22:16.081 --> 00:22:18.232
I mean, tarot dates back to
the early Christian, right?

00:22:18.267 --> 00:22:19.998
When some priests
were still using magic?

00:22:20.033 --> 00:22:21.694
And a few of them viewed
into the dark stuff.

00:22:21.729 --> 00:22:25.905
Necromancy and how to push
death away, how to cause it.

00:22:25.940 --> 00:22:28.791
So Roy's using black
magic to bind the reaper.

00:22:28.826 --> 00:22:30.986
If he is, he's riding the whirlwind.

00:22:31.021 --> 00:22:34.942
It's like putting a dog
leash on a great white.

00:22:41.083 --> 00:22:43.826
Okay, then we stop Roy. How?

00:22:43.861 --> 00:22:44.831
You know how?

00:22:44.866 --> 00:22:46.265
Wait, what the hell are
you talking about Dean?

00:22:46.300 --> 00:22:48.113
We can't kill Roy.

00:22:48.148 --> 00:22:49.301
Sam. The guy's playing god.

00:22:49.336 --> 00:22:51.953
He's deciding who lives and who
dies. That's a monster in my books.

00:22:51.988 --> 00:22:54.853
No, we're not gonna
kill a human being Dean.

00:22:54.888 --> 00:22:56.782
We do that, we're no better than he is.

00:22:56.817 --> 00:22:59.601
Okay, so we can't kill
Roy. We can't kill death.

00:22:59.636 --> 00:23:02.684
Any bright ideas college boy?

00:23:02.975 --> 00:23:04.306
Okay, uh...

00:23:04.341 --> 00:23:06.721
If Roy's using some kind
of black spell on the reaper

00:23:06.756 --> 00:23:09.149
We gotta figure out what it is.

00:23:09.184 --> 00:23:11.713
And how to break it.

00:23:16.799 --> 00:23:20.025
Service today.

00:23:24.777 --> 00:23:27.415
If Roy's using a spell.
There might be a spell book.

00:23:27.450 --> 00:23:28.617
See if you can find it.

00:23:28.652 --> 00:23:31.481
Hurry up. Services start in 15
minutes. I'll try to stroll Roy.

00:23:31.516 --> 00:23:34.259
All right. Le Grange is
a fraud. He's no healer.

00:23:34.294 --> 00:23:35.961
Amen, brother. You
keep up the good work.

00:23:35.996 --> 00:23:37.650
Thank you.

00:24:34.478 --> 00:24:36.770
Encyclopedia of Christian
History Old & New Testament

00:25:03.334 --> 00:25:08.934
Openly gay teacher wins lawsuit
Strong message sent to Nations...

00:25:19.058 --> 00:25:22.316
Wright: 'local church a cult'

00:25:31.843 --> 00:25:32.726
What have you got?

00:25:32.761 --> 00:25:34.751
Roy's choosing victims
he sees as a immoral.

00:25:34.786 --> 00:25:36.706
And I think I know
who's next on his list.

00:25:36.741 --> 00:25:38.755
Remember the protestor?
The guy in the parking lot?

00:25:38.790 --> 00:25:40.814
Yeah. Yeah, I'll find him.

00:25:40.849 --> 00:25:43.795
But you can't let Roy
heal anyone, all right?

00:26:04.410 --> 00:26:05.346
Leila.

00:26:05.381 --> 00:26:08.606
Leila Roke, come up here child.

00:26:13.896 --> 00:26:15.898
Mom... Baby.

00:26:15.933 --> 00:26:17.900
I love you.

00:26:18.950 --> 00:26:21.042
Oh, man.

00:26:30.169 --> 00:26:32.846
Leila, listen to me.
You can't get up there.

00:26:32.881 --> 00:26:34.824
Why not? We've waited for months.

00:26:34.859 --> 00:26:36.623
You can't let Roy heal you.

00:26:36.658 --> 00:26:38.671
I don't understand. Roy
healed you, didn't he?

00:26:38.706 --> 00:26:40.649
I mean, why wouldn't
you at least let him try?

00:26:40.684 --> 00:26:43.890
Because if you do, something
bad is going to happen.

00:26:43.925 --> 00:26:47.096
I can't explain. I just need
you to believe me. Leila.

00:26:47.131 --> 00:26:49.295
Please...

00:26:57.560 --> 00:26:58.972
I'm sorry.

00:26:59.007 --> 00:27:00.875
Leila. Leila!

00:27:00.910 --> 00:27:02.743
Dear child.

00:27:03.834 --> 00:27:07.019
You deserve this. I knew
the Lord would reply me...

00:27:07.054 --> 00:27:09.952
I knew the Lord would reply me.

00:27:13.421 --> 00:27:15.286
Help!

00:27:22.366 --> 00:27:24.717
Pray with me friends.

00:27:28.804 --> 00:27:31.889
I hope you're ready. I am.

00:27:42.165 --> 00:27:43.506
Help!

00:27:43.541 --> 00:27:44.899
Help me please!

00:27:44.934 --> 00:27:46.257
Where is it?

00:27:46.472 --> 00:27:48.724
It's right there!

00:27:50.157 --> 00:27:52.169
Come on, come on.

00:28:00.920 --> 00:28:02.390
Fire!

00:28:02.425 --> 00:28:04.996
The tent's on fire!

00:28:05.144 --> 00:28:07.131
Fire! Everybody get out of here!

00:28:07.166 --> 00:28:09.716
Roy! Roy, please!

00:28:09.751 --> 00:28:11.864
Please don't stop. Please!

00:28:11.899 --> 00:28:13.840
Reverend, please!

00:28:13.875 --> 00:28:15.781
Please don't stop.

00:28:15.816 --> 00:28:17.400
Please.

00:28:17.435 --> 00:28:18.950
Friends.

00:28:18.985 --> 00:28:22.561
If you all just leave the tent
in an orderly fashion and...

00:28:22.596 --> 00:28:25.269
We'll figure out what's
going on out there and...

00:28:25.304 --> 00:28:28.161
I did it. I stopped Roy.

00:28:28.196 --> 00:28:31.018
David? I think its okay.

00:28:34.768 --> 00:28:36.378
No!

00:28:36.413 --> 00:28:37.605
Dean, it didn't work!

00:28:37.640 --> 00:28:39.626
The reaper's still coming!

00:28:40.600 --> 00:28:42.143
I'm telling you... I'm telling you.

00:28:42.178 --> 00:28:44.777
It must not have worked! Roy must
not be controlling this thing!

00:28:44.812 --> 00:28:47.305
Then who the hell is?

00:28:50.356 --> 00:28:52.469
Sue Ann.

00:29:06.611 --> 00:29:08.903
Help! Help me!

00:29:09.047 --> 00:29:10.837
Help!

00:29:25.268 --> 00:29:27.591
I got you. I got you.

00:29:30.134 --> 00:29:32.118
Thank god.

00:29:37.398 --> 00:29:40.433
I just don't understand.

00:29:40.468 --> 00:29:42.231
After everything we have done for you.

00:29:42.266 --> 00:29:45.358
After Roy healed you.

00:29:46.312 --> 00:29:50.658
I'm just very very disappointed Dean.

00:29:51.994 --> 00:29:54.467
You can let him go. I'm
not gonna press charges.

00:29:54.502 --> 00:29:59.656
The Lord will deal
with him as he sees fit.

00:30:01.401 --> 00:30:02.976
We catch you around here again son.

00:30:03.011 --> 00:30:05.727
Who put the fear god in you, understand?

00:30:05.762 --> 00:30:07.494
Yes, sir. Fear god.

00:30:07.529 --> 00:30:09.348
Got it.

00:30:12.400 --> 00:30:13.932
Leila.

00:30:14.621 --> 00:30:16.244
Why would you do that Dean?

00:30:16.279 --> 00:30:18.574
It could have been my only chance.

00:30:18.609 --> 00:30:20.551
He's not a healer.

00:30:20.586 --> 00:30:22.493
He healed you.

00:30:24.131 --> 00:30:26.174
I know it doesn't seem fair.

00:30:26.209 --> 00:30:30.808
And I wish I could explain. But
Roy's not the answer, I'm sorry.

00:30:32.787 --> 00:30:35.293
Goodbye Dean.

00:30:39.870 --> 00:30:43.839
I wish you luck. I really do.

00:30:43.874 --> 00:30:46.451
Same to you.

00:30:50.427 --> 00:30:53.721
You deserve it a lot more than me.

00:30:57.074 --> 00:30:59.539
Private session tonight.
No interruptions.

00:30:59.574 --> 00:31:02.004
I give you my word.
I'll heal your daughter.

00:31:02.039 --> 00:31:05.530
Thank you, reverend. God bless you.

00:31:09.640 --> 00:31:12.913
So Roy really believes.

00:31:13.452 --> 00:31:16.101
I don't think he has any
idea what his wife's doing.

00:31:16.136 --> 00:31:20.308
Well, I found this
Hidden in their library.

00:31:20.343 --> 00:31:23.604
It's ancient. Written by a
priest who went dark side.

00:31:23.639 --> 00:31:25.678
There's a binding spell in here.

00:31:25.713 --> 00:31:27.502
For trapping a reaper.

00:31:27.537 --> 00:31:29.889
Must be hell of a spell. Yeah.

00:31:29.924 --> 00:31:33.148
You got to build a black altar
with seriously dark stuff.

00:31:33.183 --> 00:31:36.637
Bones. Human blood.

00:31:36.672 --> 00:31:40.132
To cross a line like
that. That preacher's wife.

00:31:40.167 --> 00:31:44.676
Black magic, murder, evil.

00:31:44.711 --> 00:31:46.480
Desperate.

00:31:46.515 --> 00:31:49.788
Her husband was dying. She would
have done anything to save him.

00:31:49.823 --> 00:31:53.061
She was using the binding spell
to keep the reaper away from Roy.

00:31:53.096 --> 00:31:56.701
Cheating death. Literally.

00:31:56.736 --> 00:32:00.110
Yeah, but Roy's alive so why
is she still using the spell?

00:32:00.145 --> 00:32:05.651
Right. To force the reaper to help
the people she thinks are moral.

00:32:06.655 --> 00:32:10.116
Thank god save us from half the people
who think they're doing god's work.

00:32:10.151 --> 00:32:13.714
We got to break that binding spell Dean.

00:32:15.928 --> 00:32:18.325
You know Sue Ann had to
cop a cross like this.

00:32:18.360 --> 00:32:20.687
And when she dropped it
the reaper backed off.

00:32:20.722 --> 00:32:23.599
So you think we got to find
the cross or destroy the altar.

00:32:23.634 --> 00:32:25.578
Maybe both?

00:32:26.610 --> 00:32:29.025
Whatever we do. We'd
better to do it soon.

00:32:29.060 --> 00:32:32.021
Roy's healing Leila tonight.

00:32:43.866 --> 00:32:45.742
That's Leila's car.

00:32:45.777 --> 00:32:47.618
She's already here.

00:32:47.653 --> 00:32:49.405
Yeah.

00:32:50.166 --> 00:32:52.907
Dean. You know, if Roy would
have picked Leila instead of me.

00:32:52.942 --> 00:32:55.067
She'd be healed by now. Dean, don't.

00:32:55.102 --> 00:32:57.385
And if she's not healed tonight...

00:32:57.420 --> 00:32:59.813
She's gonna die in a couple of months.

00:32:59.848 --> 00:33:02.172
What's happening to her is horrible.

00:33:02.207 --> 00:33:06.518
But what are you going to do?
Let somebody else die to save her?

00:33:06.553 --> 00:33:11.183
You said it yourself
Dean. You can't play god.

00:33:25.034 --> 00:33:26.071
Gather around.

00:33:26.106 --> 00:33:28.259
Please, everyone gather around.

00:33:28.294 --> 00:33:30.412
Come in closer. Come on up.

00:33:30.447 --> 00:33:32.704
Where's Sue Ann?

00:33:33.129 --> 00:33:35.144
House.

00:33:35.956 --> 00:33:37.464
Go find Sue Ann. I'll catch up.

00:33:37.499 --> 00:33:38.981
What are you...

00:33:40.363 --> 00:33:42.013
Hey.

00:33:42.723 --> 00:33:46.099
You're gonna put that fear god in me?

00:34:29.751 --> 00:34:31.534
See him?

00:34:31.858 --> 00:34:33.692
Na.

00:34:54.661 --> 00:34:57.086
Psycho mutt.

00:35:42.433 --> 00:35:46.579
I gave your brother a life
and I can take it away.

00:35:58.132 --> 00:36:00.042
Sam, can't you see?

00:36:00.077 --> 00:36:01.917
The Lord chose me.

00:36:01.952 --> 00:36:04.687
The reward the just
and punish the wicked.

00:36:04.722 --> 00:36:07.070
And your brother is wicked.

00:36:07.105 --> 00:36:11.485
And he deserves to die just
as Leila deserves to live.

00:36:11.520 --> 00:36:14.219
That's god's will.

00:36:16.429 --> 00:36:18.948
Goodbye Sam.

00:36:23.014 --> 00:36:24.700
Mrs. Roke.

00:36:24.735 --> 00:36:26.909
You pray with me now.

00:36:26.944 --> 00:36:29.084
Pray with me friends.

00:36:58.225 --> 00:37:00.298
All right now.

00:37:01.361 --> 00:37:04.187
All right now.

00:37:29.927 --> 00:37:31.857
All right.

00:37:57.370 --> 00:38:02.587
I don't understand. I
don't feel different.

00:38:03.425 --> 00:38:04.495
My god!

00:38:04.530 --> 00:38:06.449
What have you done?

00:38:06.484 --> 00:38:08.368
He's not your god.

00:38:08.403 --> 00:38:10.407
Reverend?

00:38:10.442 --> 00:38:12.412
Sue Ann?

00:38:58.727 --> 00:39:00.444
You okay?

00:39:00.732 --> 00:39:02.801
A little bit weak.

00:39:02.836 --> 00:39:04.472
Yeah.

00:39:05.674 --> 00:39:07.534
All right, come on.

00:39:07.569 --> 00:39:09.394
We should get going.

00:39:20.740 --> 00:39:22.834
What is it?

00:39:22.869 --> 00:39:24.928
Nothing.

00:39:26.307 --> 00:39:27.585
What is it?

00:39:27.620 --> 00:39:29.550
We did the right thing here, didn't' we?

00:39:29.585 --> 00:39:31.618
Of course we did.

00:39:31.653 --> 00:39:33.975
I didn't feel like it.

00:39:35.073 --> 00:39:36.784
I got it.

00:39:40.610 --> 00:39:44.005
Leila, come on in. Hey.

00:39:44.040 --> 00:39:45.916
Hey.

00:39:46.762 --> 00:39:48.570
How did you know we were here?

00:39:48.605 --> 00:39:50.461
Sam called.

00:39:50.496 --> 00:39:54.242
He said you wanted to say goodbye.

00:39:54.409 --> 00:39:57.423
I'm gonna grab a soda.

00:40:02.143 --> 00:40:04.268
So um...

00:40:04.303 --> 00:40:07.484
Where are you going?

00:40:07.519 --> 00:40:08.690
Don't know yet.

00:40:08.725 --> 00:40:12.769
Our work kind of takes us all over so...

00:40:14.499 --> 00:40:18.863
You know, I went back to see Roy.

00:40:18.898 --> 00:40:21.527
What happened?

00:40:22.756 --> 00:40:25.068
Nothing.

00:40:25.290 --> 00:40:31.313
He laid his hand on my
forehead. But nothing happened.

00:40:31.348 --> 00:40:33.907
I'm sorry.

00:40:34.091 --> 00:40:36.670
I'm sorry it didn't work.

00:40:36.705 --> 00:40:38.642
And Sue Ann...

00:40:38.677 --> 00:40:40.342
She's dead, you know?

00:40:40.377 --> 00:40:42.292
A stroke.

00:40:42.327 --> 00:40:45.411
Yeah, I heard.

00:40:46.068 --> 00:40:49.210
Yeah, Roy's a good man.

00:40:49.383 --> 00:40:52.614
He doesn't deserve what's happened.

00:40:55.500 --> 00:40:57.845
Must be ruff...

00:40:57.880 --> 00:41:00.250
To believe in something so much.

00:41:00.285 --> 00:41:03.665
And have it disappoint you like that.

00:41:07.801 --> 00:41:11.103
You want to hear something weird?

00:41:12.304 --> 00:41:17.131
I'm okay. Really.

00:41:17.166 --> 00:41:19.525
I guess if you're gonna have faith

00:41:19.560 --> 00:41:22.703
We can't just have it
when the miracles happen.

00:41:22.738 --> 00:41:27.978
You have to have it when they don't.

00:41:32.628 --> 00:41:36.077
So what now?

00:41:38.489 --> 00:41:42.977
God works in mysterious ways.

00:41:47.107 --> 00:41:49.479
Goodbye Dean.

00:41:51.207 --> 00:41:52.923
Hey.

00:41:58.176 --> 00:42:03.269
I'm not much of a praying type but...

00:42:04.137 --> 00:42:07.611
I'm gonna pray for you.

00:42:08.769 --> 00:42:11.118
Well...

00:42:11.284 --> 00:42:14.769
There's a miracle right there.



